    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Warp Jump Generator " hidden="false" id="17fa-dfd3-62c8-4f49">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Warp Jump Generator " typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="ca20-8f59-d130-b94c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit composed entirely of models with Warp Jump Generators may choose to set its Move Characteristic to 14” instead of moving normally. If they choose to do so, they may move in any direction ignoring Difficult, Dangerous and Impassable Terrain as though it were not present. However a unit that ends or begins its movement in Dangerous Terrain will still need to take Dangerous Terrain tests as normal, even when employing Warp Jump Generators and treats Difficult Terrain as Dangerous Terrain.

In addition to the bonus move during the Movement phase, a unit composed entirely of models with Warp jump generators may make an additional Move of 7” during the Shooting phase. This Move must be taken after the unit has completed any Shooting Attacks, is not limited by the weapons fired by the unit during that Shooting phase and ignores terrain in the same manner as moves made using a Warp Jump Generator in the Movement phase. During any Reaction that allows a unit to Move (except the Flickerjump Advanced Reaction), a unit composed entirely of models with Warp Jump Generators increases the distance of that Move by 7 and allows it to ignore terrain in the same manner as other Warp Jump Generator moves.

In addition to the bonus move during the Movement phase, a unit composed entirely of models with Warp jump generators may make an additional Move of 7” during the Shooting phase. This Move must be taken after the unit has completed any Shooting Attacks, is not limited by the weapons fired by the unit during that Shooting phase and ignores terrain in the same manner as moves made using a Warp Jump Generator in the Movement phase. During any Reaction that allows a unit to Move (except the Flickerjump Advanced Reaction), a unit composed entirely of models with Warp Jump Generators increases the distance of that Move by 7 and allows it to ignore terrain in the same manner as other Warp Jump Generator moves.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Flickerjump" id="d376-f872-a246-b859" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="5e7b-68e7-d09f-da23"/>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
